1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,500
Good morning and welcome again to Your City Today.

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:08,660
With me today is Graham Campbell, a councillor from the city council.

3
00:00:08,660 --> 00:00:14,050
He will be telling us about the plan to improve the fast-growing suburb of Red Hill.

4
00:00:14,050 --> 00:00:16,300
Good morning Graham and welcome to the show.

5
00:00:16,300 --> 00:00:17,000
Good morning, Carol.

6
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:23,300
Now, Graham, I understand that there has been a lot of community consultation for the new plan?

7
00:00:23,300 --> 00:00:27,720
Yes, we've tried to address some of the concerns that local groups told us about.

8
00:00:27,720 --> 00:00:32,291
People we've heard from are mainly worried about traffic in the area,

9
00:00:32,291 --> 00:00:36,100
and, in particular, the increasing speed of cars near schools.

10
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:41,680
They feel that it is only a matter of time before there is an accident as a lot of the children walk to the school.

11
00:00:41,680 --> 00:00:45,360
So we're trying to do something about that

12
00:00:46,020 --> 00:00:49,000
Another area of concern is the overhead power lines.

13
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:52,860
These are very old and a lot of people we spoke to asked

14
00:00:52,860 --> 00:00:54,200
if something could be done about them.

15
00:00:54,200 --> 00:01:03,160
Well, I'm happy to report that the power company have agreed to move the power lines underground at a cost of $800,000.

16
00:01:03,160 --> 00:01:07,920
I think that will really improve the look of the area, as well as being safer.

17
00:01:07,920 --> 00:01:14,540
That's good to know, but will that mean an increase in rates for the local businesses in that area?

18
00:01:14,540 --> 00:01:20,920
Well, the power company have agreed to bear the cost of this themselves after a lot of discussion with the council.

19
00:01:20,920 --> 00:01:28,840
This is wonderful news as the council now has some extra funds for us to put into other things like tree planting and art work.

20
00:01:28,840 --> 00:01:32,240
Now, we've also put together a map

21
00:01:32,240 --> 00:01:34,620
which we've sent out to all the residents in the area.

22
00:01:34,620 --> 00:01:37,380
And on the map we've marked the proposed changes.

23
00:01:37,380 --> 00:01:40,624
Firstly, we'll plant mature pine trees to provide shelter

24
00:01:40,624 --> 00:01:44,950
and shade just to the right of the supermarket in Days Road.

25
00:01:44,950 --> 00:01:48,020
In order to address the traffic problems

26
00:01:48,280 --> 00:01:51,900
the pavements on the corner of Carberry and Thomas Street be widened.

27
00:01:51,900 --> 00:01:56,360
This will help to reduce the speed of vehicles entering Thomas Street.

28
00:01:56,360 --> 00:02:01,610
We think it's very important to separate the local residential streets from the main road.

29
00:02:01,610 --> 00:02:06,800
So the roadway at the entry of Thomas Street from Days Road will be painted red.

30
00:02:06,800 --> 00:02:11,590
This should mark it more clearly and act as a signal for traffic to slow down.

31
00:02:11,590 --> 00:02:17,950
One way of making sure that the pedestrians are safe is to increase signage at the intersections.

32
00:02:17,950 --> 00:02:23,230
A 'keep clear' sign will be erected at the junction of Evelyn Street and Hill Street,

33
00:02:23,230 --> 00:02:25,870
to enable traffic to exit at all times.

34
00:02:25,870 --> 00:02:33,240
Something we're planning to do to help control the flow of traffic in the area is to install traffic lights half way down Hill Street

35
00:02:33,240 --> 00:02:35,030
where it crosses Days Road.

36
00:02:35,030 --> 00:02:39,680
Now, we haven't only thought about the cars and traffic, of course

37
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:41,760
there's also something for the children.

38
00:02:41,760 --> 00:02:45,862
We're going to get school children in the area to research a local story,

39
00:02:45,862 --> 00:02:48,620
the life of a local sports hero perhaps

40
00:02:48,940 --> 00:02:55,530
and an artist will incorporate that story into paintings on the wall of a building on the other side of Hill Street from the supermarket.

41
00:02:55,530 --> 00:02:59,049
And finally, we've agreed to build a new children's playground

42
00:02:59,049 --> 00:03:05,030
which will be at the other end of Hill Street close to the intersection with Carberry Street.

43
00:03:05,030 --> 00:03:09,400
Wonderful, now, what's the next stage?

44
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:11,640
Well, the final plan...
